From e4914821fbd4b2c568ef63285320cba23d450537 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:37:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 58/65] policy: relay spends of leaf version 0xe0 once active,
 and check them again when a tripwire goes

- SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_TRIPWIRE joins the mandatory, and so the standard,
  script verification flags, but the mempool leaves it out while the next
  block is below the activation height. There leaf version 0xe0 is still an
  unknown leaf version, and DISCOURAGE_UPGRADABLE_TAPROOT_VERSION keeps every
  spend through one at depth one or more out of the mempool, -acceptnonstdtxn
  or not. SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_EC_DISABLED is not a deployment and is in
  neither set.
- Both script checks of the mempool add SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_EC_DISABLED when
  elliptic curve checks in such leaves fail in the next block, which they
  read from the confirmed UTXO set: a tripwire output spent only in the
  mempool changes nothing until a block confirms the spend. A spend that
  fails is refused with "mempool-script-verify-flag-failed (Elliptic curve
  signature checks are disabled in this leaf)". The script execution cache
  keys on the flags and the new check comes before the signature cache, so
  neither cache carries a result across the change.
- When a block makes those checks fail for the next one, the spends through
  such leaves in the mempool are checked again under the mempool's flags for
  the next block, their inputs read through the mempool, and those that fail
  are removed with their descendants by the existing removeForReorg. A block
  connected on its own does this in ConnectTip, after the coins, the mempool
  and the tip all are the block's. During a reorganization ConnectTip does
  not: the parents some spends need are in disconnectpool then, out of the
  mempool's reach, which could let a spend through or remove a valid one,
  and the lock points of other transactions can still refer to a
  disconnected block, which removeForReorg asserts against.
  MaybeUpdateMempoolForReorg does it instead, once it has put the
  disconnected transactions back and mended the dependencies and the lock
  points, whenever the reorganized chain leaves the checks failing,
  whatever they did before, so that a resurrected parent's elliptic curve
  child goes too. ActivateBestChainStep tells ConnectTip whether it
  disconnected blocks first: disconnectpool cannot tell, since a block
  connected may confirm every transaction of the one it replaces and leave
  it empty.
- A reorganization that puts the next block below the activation height
  removes the spends through leaf version 0xe0 at depth one or more with
  their descendants, as one below the height of OP_CHECKMLDSA44 removes the
  spends that execute that opcode, which now looks at leaves of version 0xe0
  as well.
- P2MR spends through leaf version 0xe0 have the standardness rules of 0xc0
  at every height: 80-byte witness elements, except for the signature chunks
  of the two OP_CHECKMLDSA44 templates, byte for byte, at depth one or more;
  any other script that uses the opcode is not standard. Below the
  activation height that is stricter than a build without these rules for a
  spend at depth zero, which nothing executes, with a witness element above
  80 bytes. It is policy only, and it leaves the mempool without a boundary
  at the activation height past which the transactions in it would have to
  be checked again.

The flags the mempool checks with are now in one place, MempoolScriptFlags,
which PolicyScriptChecks and the checks above share.
